Z||000010||Archie||09-19-2001||12:57 AM||||Not to throw a wet towel on this..... it is necessary to have an up-front understanding.<P>Ok, I have re-read the other thread and it is my impression that this will be a "heads-up" run what you brung event to determine a "Top Dog" overall. No handicapping, no excuses.<P>If you want to break out NOS equipped cars, that's fine. But the whole idea here is that some V-6 turbo guys say they can run "Heads-Up" competitive with the SBC cars and at least one of them asked for this type of thing to happen. Actually one of them got this all started.<P>Now, I think that everyone would be welcome but, as many of you know from Fiero car show experience, there are always questions about judging and wether a particular car was properly placed in the right class. This would get real complicated when dealing with seperate classes. I think it would be best to go Heads-Up, then break out best performances by engine types, performance mods etc. make a special note of fastest N/A 4 banger and N/A 6 banger etc.<P>But Top Dog is what this is about.<P>Archie<P>BTW, I also see that the OKC event is once again scheduled opposite the Carlisle event. I wish that the OK people would reconsider the date. I would love to go to the OKC event but cannot miss Carlisle for it.<P>Archie<P>Let's get it on!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Just how fast do you want to go?||||reg||1
Z||000011||Turbo88||09-19-2001||01:10 AM||||My arguement in the other thread is that I can build a turbo'ed V6 that will beat any naturally aspirated V8 and do it for the same money as what it costs to build a motor and kit and put it into a fiero. If you drop a 500 shot of juice into a SBC well, that moves things into a different perspective. The powerfest idea I brought forward was based on that heads up and autox style racing but it seems that there will be a lot that V8s and turbo6s. I think it would be fair to include them. But don't worry, the original spirit is there. Well put BTW...<P>Lets Get it on!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cheever3000||09-19-2001||01:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>BTW, I also see that the OKC event is once again scheduled opposite the Carlisle event.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Don't rely on the information I posted.  I'm not a member of the host club, and not involved in the planning & administration of it in any way.  I was just looking at my notes in <I>this year's</I> PFF calendar.  Nothing different has come my way, so I'm going on the last info available.<P><BR>||||reg||1
