Z||000024||Slammed Fiero||09-19-2001||12:08 PM||||I think we need to develop at least some sort of classification. Street cars , competition cars , ect. <P>Ie.<BR>Stock classes<BR>S1 cars 84 to 87 4cyl<BR>S2 cars 84 to 87 6cyl<BR>S3 cars 88 4cyl<BR>s4 cars 88 v6<P>Street modified (SM) probably the biggest class only denoted by SM you can run DOT approved slicks such as BFG drag radials , Nitto drag tires , Kumoho Victoracers , Hoosier radials , ToyoRA1's. no competition only tires. These cars must have up to date registration and insurance on them.<P><BR>Competition cars. Free for all, drag slicks , trailered cars , ect ect.<P>I kept the stock class seperated by year because in stock form an 88 does handle better than an 84 to 87 variant. But in Street mod year doesn't really matter.<P>I know some guys with dedicated autocrossers that would blow the doors of anyone in the forum (George Ryans old car, Greg Duncan team python) but would pull a mid 13 at the strip. By the sounds of some of the cars on the forum a mid 13 sec run would put you in the middle of the pack. With the fastest drag car honours going to the customer on Archies page running in the 10's (documented)<P>Good examples of street cars 1FST2m6's , my car , Sluppy , anyone running a street turbo setup ,  small blocks. Cars running in a street class should have to be driven there.<P>Could run a stock class for 4 and 6cyl cars , with lets say 3 minor mods allowed. Coil would be free be , K&N filters , ect, ect. I know a stock 86 GT that runs 15.2's through the lights with only a K&N filter. Try and beat that with your stock GT if you think you can<P>could have an award for the fastest 4,6, and 8 cyl cars. I think 1FST2m6 has shown us that top honours may not always go to a 3.4 3800 or a 4.3. You would have to divide the cars into a power added , Non power added car. (NOS, turbo's supercharger are power adders)<P>If there is any money involved it should go to the all around best contender. that 10 sec drag car on archies page would no doubt kill in the drags , but lets see it in an autocross.  Same goes for a purpose built autocrosser not being a monster at the strip.<P><BR>No front engined cheese wagons.<P>This is just an idea , I have been around Corvair autocrosses and PCA events and I have seen how they classify cars.<P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, Big Bore TB, 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000025||MinnGreenGT||09-19-2001||12:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B><P>No front engined cheese wagons.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What about Boomtastic?  Bring on the front engine!!! I want to see it!  Umm cheese wagons? (no front-engine cars from Wisconsin?)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
