Z||000035||Jay||09-19-2001||07:49 PM||||Yes, just what I've been waiting for.  Set a date as soon as possible so I can make arrangements.  Just did a 13.4 @102mph<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000036||lildevil||09-19-2001||08:16 PM||||If you get this worked out... I AM THERE! Been trying to put something like this together out here on the East Coast but there seems to be no interest.  WHat you need to do is contact High Performance MAgazine. They've been looking for some new Pontiac articles to run about shootouts. If there is enough interest and a track available they will flip the bill for the track for the day. Only problem i could see is the distance but if you set a date enough ahead of time and we get some convoys goin i think it would be ok. As for the classes...this is how they do  it at the track i go to. Run a Quick 8. EVERY car there runs qualifying runs. Say 3 to 4 runs. The 8 fastest cars (determined by qualifing rounds) go into a sepearte class.  The remaining cars can then be seperated into classes determined by engine....or turned into a bracket race (handicapped) so those with slower cars will be more intersted in attending. Also make the date in the cooler Spring months or Fall. Better times that way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000037||vEnOm||09-19-2001||09:38 PM||||That’s an excellent idea. Too bad Im stuck down here with Drex. Sheesh! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Venom||||reg||6
Z||000038||Archie||09-19-2001||10:50 PM||||You know, IMHO, this is getting a bit out of hand for an event that is just in the talking stages. No offense ment to anyone. Some of these posts have this thing broken down into 27 classes covering every posible combination of parts that can be put on a Fiero. I even saw where someone wants to break the 6 bangers into classes based on engine size etc. Please let's not get this thing so complicated that the concept fails under it's own weight. Don't make it so much work to administer that the person putting it all together doesn't have time to race his own car.<P>This started out as a talk about wether a Turbo V-6 can beat a N/A SBC. Now it's a multi-class event with talk of trophies, overall cash prizes etc. When this discussion started I had in my mind an idea of how this event would go down. What I was thinking about was a way to make an event that had something for everybody but still allowed the "Head to Head, No Excuses" Top Dog Shoot Out. Now my plan hadn't considered NOS equipped cars and that is the only subject that makes a competition formula difficult. So NOS has yet to be addressed.<P>And it seems that great minds think alike. My plan (if you call it that) was just like Earl  Sessions has described. Except that I had figured on a "Quick 16". I also thought the same formula would work for the autocross cars. Other than that my plan or vision was just as he describes except that somehow we have to address NOS equipped cars. Maybe we could ask that they not run the NOS during the event then let them put on a little show WITH NOS at the end, dunno.<P>If you will re-read my previous posts, you'll see that I also have been thinking for several years that I'd like to get some of my customers together for like a "V-8 Reunion" (kinda like the Saturn Reunions they had). One of the greatest rewards I get from providing V-8 kits to people is the thrill of meeting and talking to them at events or shows. That is why, at the shows, I don't set up a booth and sit there and try to Hawk my wares. I Go around and try to meet people both new and old. When they are ready to buy, they will buy, they don't need me sitting there at a table leaning on them to buy today. In an effort to further the idea of meeting more of my customers, I decided to offer $ 500 to the highest placing V-8 Archie equipped car. (I'm still considering the with/without NOS question, Jimmy) I've seen talk of my  money should be going to a pot for overall winners or something like that. That won't be happening, it's the highest placing V-8 Archie equipped car. <P>The main thing here is that this was supposed to determine, once and for all, if a properly built Turbo V-6 car can keep up with a N/A SBC car. If a NStar or 2 show up that's even better yet, we can settle the NStar vs SBC arguement at that time also. While I figure that the more the better, everyone welcome is fine with me. This was never about a class for everyone, everyone wins a trophy, everyone competes within a class structure. This was about a Run what you brung, heads up, put up or shut up, no excuses, RACE. The winner would have ALL of the Bragging rights. The 2nd place LOSER, would be just that, a loser with no excuses. <P>Now, I'm not trying to be nasty & I'm not trying to exclude interested persons from having fun. AND I'm certainly not trying to flame anyone. But, It needs to be understood that this event has the potential to quiet the 14 threads per day that ask what is faster.<P>Now, let's keep it in perspective and race the dang cars.<P>Now on the subject of tracks.... I know that the Publishing company that puts out Kit Car Illustrated Magazine also owns the racing complex just east of St. Louis in Collinsville IL. That Publishing Company also owns several other automotive magazines, wouldn't it be nice if that also owned the Magazine that Earl is talking about?<P>I hope this helps and also clearly states my position without hurting anyone's feelings.<P>Archie<P>Sorry for re-posting so much of Earl's post below, but he said it so well. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lildevil:<BR><B> WHat you need to do is contact High Performance MAgazine. They've been looking for some new Pontiac articles to run about shootouts. If there is enough interest and a track available they will flip the bill for the track for the day. Only problem i could see is the distance but if you set a date enough ahead of time and we get some convoys goin i think it would be ok. As for the classes...this is how they do  it at the track i go to. Run a Quick 8. EVERY car there runs qualifying runs. Say 3 to 4 runs. The 8 fastest cars (determined by qualifing rounds) go into a sepearte class.  The remaining cars can then be seperated into classes determined by engine....or turned into a bracket race (handicapped) so those with slower cars will be more intersted in attending. Also make the date in the cooler Spring months or Fall. Better times that way   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000039||Mach10||09-19-2001||10:52 PM||||Hell, *I* might even be able to make it. I'll bring Box'N'Battle gloves to settle gudges  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Can't see myself running more than stock, though. <BR>Still, I'd be there to see some smoke, lots of rubber, maybe an exploding kit or two  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Nothing like a v-8 tearing free of it's mounts, and finding it's own way down the track(for a track-best-time), or a turbo fragging, and the ensuing scavenger hunt for the runnaway impeller(whoever finds it gets a bag of Circus Peanuts)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Good Clean Wholesome Fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>I say it's for the FUN... I'll be there if I can, and Bunsen-Burner will be ready to ROCK  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000040||NOS3800||09-19-2001||11:11 PM||||Hey, NOS powered cars are people TOO! Naw, I understand why you wouldn't want to include NOS powered cars, but hey, I must disagree. Its the same as having a turbo or SC on a car. Maybe in the Turbo V6 vs V8 competition should be set apart from the rest with no NOS allowed so they can settle their dispute. Everyone else can be lumped together with Quick 16 classes. We have to keep it simple though. Just let everyone compete no matter what they have in their cars. If need be, just make a NOS class! I would love for that to happen. All motors that spray would be in this class. Spectators can place bets on who blows their motor FIRST! DOH!<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.45@101.12 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BillCar2001_4.jpg"> ||||reg||8
Z||000041||Archie||09-19-2001||11:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NOS3800:<BR><B> If need be, just make a NOS class! I would love for that to happen. All motors that spray would be in this class. Spectators can place bets on who blows their motor FIRST! DOH!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's a good idea...... I just wanna be in the 1st row to watch.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000042||Formula88||09-19-2001||11:34 PM||||Split it up however you want, and then have the winner of each class run eliminators against each other till one winner is left.  The Fastest Fiero.  That's what everyone wants to find out about, right?||||reg||3
Z||000043||Turbo88||09-20-2001||12:40 AM||||Sinse I am guilty of making this a grudge match benchracing event turned power show, let me clear a couple things. The only money that has been mentioned has been Archie and I offering 500 bucks to the fastest person running our respective kits. If I sell enough of them and can get some of the other Fiero businesses to pony up a couple bucks, I thought about having a few trophies made up. <P>This whole thing is designed to settle some long running bench races over turbo/nos/Northstar/sbc who is the baddest on the block arguement. It will be grudge matches and it will be heads up. If enough people commit to coming and we get the details worked out (funding ect), then I think we should have some simple classes but nothing so complicated as we have 2 cars per class and cars running in 17 different classes. I envision a lot of 'lets get it on, line em up and run' with some ever so slight level of matching cars up so we aren't running the stock duke guys against a blown and injected small block with the sneaky pete bottle of juice hidden in a frame rail. However, if that 4 banger wants to run that sbc, then more power to him. <P>If we are going to rent the track, that will cost money so we need to come up with entry fee schedule. Also, if any of you super nice fiero type people out there want to help out with some of the details, all the cooler. I am also going to try to drum up some local sponsership and see if I can some coverage of the event. If anyone knows someone at a hipo mag, once we set a date, give em a call and see what they say! Feel free to email me suggestions (easier to track than forum messages). <P>If we get as many hotrod Fieros as have expressed interest, this ought to be one hell of a show.<P>-Bryan<P>||||reg||1
Z||000044||GT Bastard||09-20-2001||04:40 AM||||COUNT ME IN!  I'm bringing my '86SE V6.  Me and 1FST2M6 need to have a grudge match.  That would kick A$$(assuming he forgets to use his NOS...hehe.)<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtbastard.gif">     <P>"My heroes are John Wayne, the Simpsons, and whoever canceled Full House/Bob Saget."||||reg||1
Z||000045||MinnGreenGT||09-20-2001||10:06 AM||||Stick with the Archie-plan. Think of the KISS principle (Keep It Simple Stupid) and not let things get out of hand!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
