Z||000050||lildevil||09-20-2001||08:11 PM||||Heres another idea.  There are several ALLL PONTIAC drag races and shows throughout the country. The shows held at Englishtown NJ and Maple Grove PA come to mind.  I believe there is a big one held in Ohio?  Called AMES Pontaic show?  Anyone know what i am talking about?  We would contact the director of one of these show and ask if they will make a seperate Fiero class.  We all run in the class no matter what it is that powers our cars. V-8's to 4 cyls. to FLUX Capacitors.Our leverage in this situation is that the show directors would love to see as many cars as possible show up....so if we show up with 50-100 fieros and we all pay to get and join the program we have lots of leverage to do what we wish. i would think.  <P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
