Z||000089||West Coast Fiero||12-16-2001||11:38 PM||||not to mention I would feel alot more comfortable on the first annual event if several Fiero vendor locations such as Archie's and Ed Parks were on the places to visit should there be any mechanical troubles<BR> <BR>but also here are the benifits of doing it this way - <B>still these are just sugestions</B><P><BR><LI> Each place can act as a waypoint, or check-in to establish who is in the lead in each class<BR><LI> benifit of visiting and establishing relations with the Fiero vendors that we normally wouldnt meet due to geographics<BR><LI> it would make for shorter trips for each  run thereby making for more time to rest, party, drink, socialize, oogle over Fiero Lisa     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drool.gif"> , etc.<BR><LI> The event would last longer than a single run, making it more worth while for those coming from across the country or even internationally ( hint, hint, AusFiero )<P><BR> If there are any more ideas, this is the best media to get them down on, we then can establish who will be setting up the perameters and who will be in charge of the event. One thing to make sure of is to call each county of every place planned to be visitied on the trip and inform Law Enforcement of the event so as they are not over whelmed with traffic situations and know what to expect, as well as all Chambers of Commerce.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif">    <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>[This message has been edited by West Coast Fiero (edited 12-16-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by West Coast Fiero (edited 12-16-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by West Coast Fiero (edited 12-16-2001).]||||reg||1
