Z||000091||West Coast Fiero||12-17-2001||12:20 AM||||just from past experiences in my own club ( Fieros West ) <A HREF="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest" TARGET=_blank>http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest</A>  it takes some major voice raising and almost comes down to fist fights to get people to do <B>ANYTHING</B><P> but is something like this happens and especially with the encouragement of <FONT COLOR="red"><B>WCF</B></FONT> there would be a significant amount of folks here from the west coast the would consider attending<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000092||fieroX||12-17-2001||04:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B>[b]JUST A THOUGHT........</B><P> but from what I have seen in Hot Rod magazine thier Power Tour begins from where they left off the previous year. <BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>In 1999 the tour started in San Bernardino california, and ended in Nashville, TN.  In 2000 it started In cali and ended in panama city fl.  In 2001 it started in detroit and ended in San berdo, and in 2002 it will start in Nebraska, and end in Ohio.<BR>But anyway Im up for whatever it takes to get this event rolling.  I think the idea to host it where assistance is available if needed is a great idea.  I think we should find a venue that isnt just a drag strip though.  I really to see autoX racing also.  It will attract alot more people, and really find the fastest fiero, not just in the corners, or on the strip, but both!||||reg||1
