Z||000096||Haze_Performance||12-17-2001||06:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>So, Archie & Turbo88 are you sick of our suggestions yet?  Why haven't you posted?  As you can see there is much enthusiasm for this "event."</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I think that they wanted Turbo 6 vs. V8 only. This was going to be there event to show how those engines compare. After reading the topic everyone wanted a class to race in. (me included  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) It may have gotten them a little upset being that this topic went so far off of there original idea..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">      <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">1984 Indy For Sale ~ <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000097||lildevil||12-17-2001||07:02 PM||||Jus a thought but the AMES All Pontiac show and drag race is the second week of August this year in Ohio. Theres 3 days of drag racing. Wouldn't it be soooooo much easier jus having everyone show up to this event? All ready has magazine coverage. The Racing is all ready set up.  And its a show. Its in a central location...maybe not for those on the west coast.  <P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000098||Old Lar||12-17-2001||08:45 PM||||I've always heard you don't drive your race car to the track.  When FOCOA had the nationals in St Louis, all participants were excited about the opportunity to run on Gateway International Raceway, which Phil had gotten for a day.  Excited that is until they found out the cost was $50/car.  The track was $5000 for the day, 100 cars would pay for it. To hear the show participants it was like selling their fisrt born, and it was too expensive, and why should it cost so much..yada yada yada.<P>I had fun running my car, but it cost Phil a bundle because of the no shows.  The cost was still $5000 for the track.  Only a couple of cars broke during the day one was Fiero Doc's 3.4 whose engine went, another lost a transmission.<BR>So before anyone gets the idea for renting out a track for a Fiero day, keep it in mind there are a lot of people who wont put the money where their mouth is.  The better idea is to go to a track like Englishtown during Hi Peformance Pontiac Day and run for those who bring the cash to race.  I've been there, but not to race.  It would be too long a drive back home to fix someting if it broke.||||reg||1
Z||000099||Joe Torma||12-17-2001||08:45 PM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B> <BR>I think that they wanted Turbo 6 vs. V8 only. This was going to be there event to show how those engines compare. After reading the topic everyone wanted a class to race in. (me included      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) It may have gotten them a little upset being that this topic went so far off of there original idea..      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, I'm very guilty...because I don't think you can crown "the fastest Fiero in the land" without inviting all the Fieros in the land.  It may not be a turbo6 or SBC that wins.<P>[Edit]I reread this thread some...looks like Turbo88 is holding it in Saint Louis MO.<P>Sorry to complicate and annoy.<BR>I'm leaving this thread alone now. ok,bye   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 12-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000100||NOS3800||12-17-2001||10:42 PM||||I am in agreement with Old Lar. I have tried getting a bunch of Fieros together for an event like this and never get the numbers that are expected, I think we on the EastCoast should use the Englishtown Pontiac Day as our Run and Gun type event. Its all set up already, has magazine coverage( I will get with HPP to get a Fiero only Class if they don't have one). The most Fieros we got was last summer. We had around ten racing. But we didn't get the word out. Maybe have a West Coast event, a Mid-America event and an East Coast event, then compare numbers here. Its hard for alot of the members to travel such distances, especially if there is a chance of breaking.<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000101||cadero2dmax||12-17-2001||10:45 PM||||I have a couple questions, and a couple suggestions to accompany the questions.<P>What kind of competition? It could be patterned after the Grassroots Motorsports Challenge, which has a compound score for the drag race, plus an autocross event, and a judging. If the event were held here in Tulsa sometime, I think I could put together an event at Hallett, for some road course work in addition (using my afilliation with N.A.S.A. for sanctioning and insurance).<P>G||||reg||1
